      "path": "cli/README.md",
      "content": "# openguardrails\n\nThe command behind [OpenGuardrails](../README.md).\n\n```text\nopenguardrails serve                    the local service: OGR Runtime API, and the model gateway if configured\nopenguardrails status                   check the service, every upstream, the model API and AIRS; exit 1 on a problem\nopenguardrails connect                  turn on the model: get a free key, and show where to claim more\nopenguardrails decisions                what the rules and the model decided, with no arguments or message text\nopenguardrails run -- <command...>      run a command and everything it spawns inside the sandbox\nopenguardrails log [run-id]             what a sandboxed run did\nopenguardrails stop                     stop the local service\n```\n\nConfiguration is `~/.openguardrails/config.json`, mode 0600. Every part is optional:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"workspaces\": [\"/Users/me/work\"],\n  \"model\": { \"apiKeyEnv\": \"OPENGUARDRAILS_API_KEY\", \"failMode\": \"closed\" },\n  \"gateway\": {\n    \"upstreams\": { \"primary\": { \"baseURL\": \"http://10.0.0.5:8000/v1\", \"model\": \"dsv41-flash\", \"apiKey\": \"local-no-auth\" } },\n    \"routes\": { \"auto\": [\"primary\"] }\n  },\n  \"sandbox\": { \"allowHosts\": [\"10.0.0.5:8888\"] }\n}\n```\n\n- `workspaces` are the absolute directories an agent works in. A relative path is taken as inside\n  one. An absolute path outside them goes to the model. The Runtime API does not tell this service an\n  agent's working directory, so nothing else can draw this line yet.\n- The local service listens on loopback and takes any API key. Avoid port 4190: `fetch` refuses it, so every\n  agent built on Node would fail to connect while `curl` works.\n\n## What the rules decide\n\n| Answer | Examples |\n|---|---|\n| allow | `git status`, `grep -rn TODO src`, reading or changing a file in the workspace, the agent's own bookkeeping |\n| deny | `rm -rf /`, formatting a disk, reading `~/.ssh/id_rsa` or `~/.aws/credentials`, cloud metadata endpoints, changing this tool's own configuration |\n| the model decides | everything else: network, installs, `git push`, deleting, scripts, `.env`, `.git/hooks`, `package.json`, any tool the rules do not know |\n\nNothing that leaves the machine is ever allowed by a rule.\n\n## Two ways to connect\n\n**The gateway, recommended.** Point the agent's base URL at `http://127.0.0.1:4180/v1`. Every request\npasses through it, whichever harness sent it. It holds your provider keys, masks secrets on the way\nout and judges tool calls on the way back. With AIRS configured, AIRS does the masking and judging.\n\n**A plugin**, from `integrations/agent/`, with `OGR_RUNTIME_URL=http://127.0.0.1:4180`. A refused call\nreaches the agent as a failed tool call, so it carries on by itself. But a plugin sees only what its\nharness shows it. Tested: on Hermes the request that names a session goes out unmasked, on OpenClaw\n2026.6 no model traffic reaches the plugin's interceptor, and the DeepSeek Harness plugin does not load\non 0.2.0-rc.2. A plugin that fails to load can leave the agent running with no guard and one line of\nwarning.\n\n## What it does not do yet\n\n- **A refused step can end the agent's turn.** Through the gateway, a refused call is removed from the\n  reply and the reason added to its text. If no call survives, the turn ends with that reason, for\n  the person to read. It does not end the session. If another call survives, the task goes on.\n- A rule reads one action. The model sees the whole session, but only for the actions that reach it.\n- With no model connected, what the rules cannot decide proceeds unjudged, subject to the agent's own\n  permission check. It is logged as `unjudged`. The same goes for a used-up quota, and the person is told\n  once a day.\n- Once connected, a model that cannot answer means the action is refused, and the agent is told it may\n  retry. Set `\"failMode\": \"open\"` under `model` to let such actions through instead.\n- **Placeholders do not survive a restart of the service.** A model that reuses one from before gets\n  that call refused, with an explanation, and no tool sees the placeholder.\n- A secret the rules do not recognize is not masked. Prose in a reply keeps its placeholders, on\n  purpose: only a tool gets the real value.\n- The gateway sees what is sent to it. An agent or a tool that calls a provider directly goes around it.\n  `openguardrails run` forces the network through this machine's proxy and records that traffic.\n- Only OpenAI Chat is tested against real harnesses. Anthropic Messages streaming is tested against a\n  stand-in. On OpenAI Responses a refusal in a stream retracts the whole step.\n- `openguardrails run` hides this tool's own configuration from the sandbox, so a plugin inside it\n  cannot read a key from there. Pass the local service's address to the plugin instead.\n\n## Sandbox and gateway\n\n`openguardrails run` uses [`@anthropic-ai/sandbox-runtime`](https://github.com/anthropics/sandbox-runtime):\nSeatbelt on macOS, bubblewrap and seccomp on Linux. It is a beta, so the version is pinned, and its\nstated limits apply. macOS also needs `ripgrep`. Linux needs `bubblewrap`, `socat` and `ripgrep`.\nWindows is untested.\n\nThe gateway also fails over between model APIs, for OpenAI Chat, OpenAI\nResponses and Anthropic Messages. It does not translate protocols, so the members of a route must\nspeak the protocol their client speaks.\n\n## Experiments\n\n```sh\nnpm run build\nexperiments/run.sh <hermes|openclaw|dsh> <empty-lab-dir> [gateway|live|judge|nomodel]\n```\n\nRuns the real harness in a throwaway home, against a scripted model and a scripted model API: through\nthe gateway with `gateway`, through the gateway and a real Model API at `$MODEL_API_URL` with `live`, or\nwith its plugin otherwise. Files in the work directory prove what really ran. The harness must already be installed.\n\nThe secret rules in `rules/secrets.json` are a snapshot of what OpenGuardrails AIRS serves. Every rule\ncarries examples, and the tests fail if one stops passing them. Examples shaped like a real issuer's key\nare left out of this public file and assembled in the tests instead.\n"
    },
    {
      "path": "cli/package.json",
      "content": "{\n  \"name\": \"openguardrails\",\n  \"version\": \"7.0.0\",\n  \"description\": \"AI agent guardrails for every builder: local rules, a sandbox and a firewall for your agents, with the OpenGuardrails model for the calls rules cannot make.\",\n  \"license\": \"Apache-2.0\",\n  \"type\": \"module\",\n  \"repository\": { \"type\": \"git\", \"url\": \"git+https://github.com/openguardrails/openguardrails.git\", \"directory\": \"cli\" },\n  \"homepage\": \"https://openguardrails.com\",\n  \"keywords\": [\"ai-agent\", \"guardrails\", \"agent-security\", \"claude-code\", \"codex\", \"sandbox\", \"firewall\", \"auto-mode\"],\n  \"bin\": { \"openguardrails\": \"dist/src/cli.js\", \"ogr\": \"dist/src/cli.js\" },\n  \"files\": [\"dist/src\", \"rules\", \"LICENSE\", \"README.md\"],\n  \"engines\": { \"node\": \">=22.12.0\" },\n  \"scripts\": {\n    \"build\": \"tsc && chmod +x dist/src/cli.js\",\n    \"test\": \"npm run build && node --test \\\"dist/test/*.test.js\\\"\",\n    \"prepublishOnly\": \"npm test\"\n  },\n  \"dependencies\": { \"@anthropic-ai/sandbox-runtime\": \"0.0.81\" },\n  \"devDependencies\": { \"@types/node\": \"^22.0.0\", \"typescript\": \"^5.6.0\" }\n}\n"
    },
    {
      "path": "cli/src/cli.ts",
      "content": "#!/usr/bin/env node\nimport { existsSync, readFileSync } from \"node:fs\";\nimport { join } from \"node:path\";\nimport { homeDir } from \"./config.js\";\nimport { latestRun, readRun, renderEvent } from \"./record.js\";\nimport { connect } from \"./connect.js\";\nimport { run } from \"./run.js\";\nimport { serve, status, stop } from \"./serve.js\";\n\nconst USAGE = `openguardrails: AI agent guardrails for every builder\n\n  openguardrails connect [--url <url>]   turn on the model: get a free key, and show where to claim more\n  openguardrails decisions               print what the rules and the model decided, newest last\n  openguardrails run [options] -- <command...>   run a command and everything it spawns inside the sandbox\n  openguardrails log [run-id]                    print what a run did (default: the latest)\n  openguardrails status                          check the gateway, every upstream and AIRS; exit 1 on a problem\n  openguardrails serve                           run the local service in the foreground (\\`run\\` starts it for you)\n  openguardrails stop                            stop the local service, for instance after editing the config\n\nrun options:\n  --enforce              deny every host not allowed, instead of recording it\n  --allow-host <host>    allow a host; an IP needs a port (--allow-host 10.0.0.5:8888)\n  --deny-host <host>     deny a host in every mode\n  --allow-read <path>    re-open a credential path that is denied by default\n  --allow-write <path>   allow writes outside the project, temp and agent state directories\n  --allow-local-bind     let the command listen on a local port, for agents with a web UI\n\nConfiguration is ~/.openguardrails/config.json. See the README.\n`;\n\nfunction parseRun(args: string[]) {\n  const options = { enforce: false, allowLocalBinding: false, allowHosts: [] as string[], denyHosts: [] as string[], allowRead: [] as string[], allowWrite: [] as string[], command: [] as string[] };\n  const lists: Record<string, string[]> = {\n    \"--allow-host\": options.allowHosts,\n    \"--deny-host\": options.denyHosts,\n    \"--allow-read\": options.allowRead,\n    \"--allow-write\": options.allowWrite,\n  };\n  for (let i = 0; i < args.length; i += 1) {\n    const arg = args[i]!;\n    if (arg === \"--\") {\n      options.command = args.slice(i + 1);\n      break;\n    }\n    if (arg === \"--enforce\") {\n      options.enforce = true;\n      continue;\n    }\n    if (arg === \"--allow-local-bind\") {\n      options.allowLocalBinding = true;\n      continue;\n    }\n    const list = lists[arg];\n    const value = args[i + 1];\n    if (!list || value === undefined) throw new Error(`unknown or incomplete option: ${arg}`);\n    list.push(value);\n    i += 1;\n  }\n  if (options.command.length === 0) throw new Error(\"nothing to run: openguardrails run -- <command...>\");\n  return options;\n}\n\nasync function main(argv: string[]): Promise<number> {\n  const [verb, ...rest] = argv;\n  if (verb === \"run\") return run(parseRun(rest));\n  if (verb === \"serve\") return serve();\n  if (verb === \"status\") return status();\n  if (verb === \"stop\") return stop();\n  if (verb === \"connect\") {\n    const at = rest.indexOf(\"--url\");\n    return connect(at >= 0 ? rest[at + 1] : undefined);\n  }\n  if (verb === \"decisions\") {\n    const path = join(homeDir(), \"decisions.ndjson\");\n    if (existsSync(path)) process.stdout.write(readFileSync(path, \"utf8\"));\n    return 0;\n  }\n  if (verb === \"log\") {\n    const runId = rest[0] ?? latestRun();\n    if (!runId) throw new Error(\"no runs recorded yet\");\n    for (const event of readRun(runId)) console.log(renderEvent(event));\n    return 0;\n  }\n  process.stdout.write(USAGE);\n  return verb && verb !== \"help\" && verb !== \"--help\" ? 2 : 0;\n}\n\nmain(process.argv.slice(2)).then(\n  (code) => process.exit(code),\n  (error) => {\n    // Refusing is the rule: a command that starts without the firewall only looks protected.\n    process.stderr.write(`[openguardrails] ${error instanceof Error ? error.message : String(error)}\\n`);\n    process.exit(1);\n  },\n);\n"
    },
    {
      "path": "cli/src/decide.ts",
      "content": "/**\n * The local layer: one tool call in, one of three answers out, no network and no model.\n *\n *   allow  It runs. The action is read-only or stays inside the workspace.\n *   deny   It does not run, and no model or agent can change that.\n *   judge  The model decides, because a rule cannot.\n */\nimport { resolve, sep } from \"node:path\";\nimport { gateCommand, HARD_CREDENTIAL, SENSITIVE_PATH, type GateDecision } from \"./gate/gate.js\";\nimport { pathOf, shellLine, toolKind } from \"./tools.js\";\n\nexport interface DecideOptions {\n  /** Absolute directories the agent works in. Relative paths are taken as inside. */\n  workspaces?: readonly string[];\n}\n\nexport interface ToolCallInput {\n  name: string;\n  args: Record<string, unknown>;\n}\n\n/**\n * Inside a workspace, but what is written here runs later or changes the rules: hooks, CI, build\n * scripts, agent configuration and shell startup files. So \"inside the workspace\" is not enough.\n */\nconst PROTECTED_WRITE =\n  /(^|\\/)(\\.git|\\.husky|\\.github\\/workflows|\\.gitlab-ci\\.yml|\\.claude|\\.codex|\\.hermes|\\.openclaw|\\.dsh|\\.openguardrails|\\.vscode|\\.idea|\\.mcp\\.json|\\.envrc|\\.npmrc|\\.bashrc|\\.zshrc|\\.zshenv|\\.zprofile|\\.profile|\\.bash_profile|package\\.json|Makefile|makefile|justfile|Dockerfile|setup\\.py|pyproject\\.toml|conftest\\.py|CLAUDE\\.md|AGENTS\\.md|SOUL\\.md)(\\/|$)/;\n\nfunction inWorkspace(path: string, workspaces: readonly string[]): boolean {\n  if (path.startsWith(\"~\")) return false;\n  if (!path.startsWith(\"/\")) return !path.split(\"/\").includes(\"..\");\n  const target = resolve(path);\n  return workspaces.some((root) => target === resolve(root) || target.startsWith(resolve(root) + sep));\n}\n\nexport function decideTool(call: ToolCallInput, options: DecideOptions = {}): GateDecision {\n  const workspaces = options.workspaces ?? [];\n  const kind = toolKind(call.name);\n  if (kind === \"internal\") return { verdict: \"allow\", reason: \"the agent's own bookkeeping\" };\n\n  if (kind === \"shell\") {\n    const line = shellLine(call.args);\n    if (!line) return { verdict: \"judge\", reason: \"a shell tool with no readable command\" };\n    return gateCommand(line, { workspaces });\n  }\n\n  if (kind === \"read\" || kind === \"search\" || kind === \"write\") {\n    const path = pathOf(call.args) ?? (kind === \"search\" ? \".\" : null);\n    if (!path) return { verdict: \"judge\", reason: `${call.name} names no path` };\n    if (/\\.openguardrails(\\/|$)/.test(path)) {\n      return kind === \"write\" ? { verdict: \"deny\", reason: \"changing OpenGuardrails' own configuration\" } : { verdict: \"judge\", reason: \"reading OpenGuardrails' own configuration\" };\n    }\n    if (kind !== \"search\" && HARD_CREDENTIAL.test(path)) return { verdict: \"deny\", reason: \"reading or changing a private key or cloud credential\" };\n    if (SENSITIVE_PATH.test(path)) return { verdict: \"judge\", reason: \"a path where secrets live\" };\n    if (!inWorkspace(path, workspaces)) return { verdict: \"judge\", reason: \"a path outside the workspace\" };\n    if (kind === \"write\" && PROTECTED_WRITE.test(path)) return { verdict: \"judge\", reason: \"a file that runs later or changes the rules\" };\n    return { verdict: \"allow\", reason: kind === \"write\" ? \"a change inside the workspace\" : \"a read inside the workspace\" };\n  }\n\n  return { verdict: \"judge\", reason: `${call.name} is not a tool the rules understand` };\n}\n"
    },
    {
      "path": "cli/src/gateway.ts",
      "content": "/**\n * The gateway: one local base URL in front of many model APIs, trying them in order.\n * It rewrites the model name and the key and nothing else: it does not translate protocols, so\n * the members of a route must speak the protocol their client speaks.\n */\nimport { randomBytes } from \"node:crypto\";\nimport { appendFileSync, mkdirSync, writeFileSync } from \"node:fs\";\nimport http, { type IncomingHttpHeaders, type IncomingMessage, type ServerResponse } from \"node:http\";\nimport https from \"node:https\";\nimport { hostname, userInfo } from \"node:os\";\nimport { join } from \"node:path\";\nimport { StringDecoder } from \"node:string_decoder\";\nimport zlib from \"node:zlib\";\nimport { INTEGRATION } from \"./airs.js\";\nimport { homeDir, resolveRoute, secretOf, type Config, type Upstream } from \"./config.js\";\nimport { ExecTracker, type ExecReport, type Observation } from \"./exec.js\";\nimport { ModelChannelGuard, type GuardedRequest } from \"./guard.js\";\nimport { handleRuntime, LocalRuntime } from \"./runtime.js\";\nimport { classifyModelRequest, harnessFrom, hostsIn, toolCallsIn, toolCallsInReply, toolResultIdsIn, type LlmProtocol } from \"./model.js\";\n\ntype Gateway = NonNullable<Config[\"gateway\"]>;\n\n/** The request's fault: another upstream would refuse it too, so it goes back to the client. */\nexport const isFailoverStatus = (status: number) => status >= 500 || [401, 403, 404, 408, 429].includes(status);\n\nexport function rewriteBody(body: Record<string, any>, upstream: Upstream): Record<string, any> {\n  const out: Record<string, any> = { ...body, model: upstream.model };\n  const kwargs = body.chat_template_kwargs;\n  if (upstream.renameTemplateKwargs && kwargs && typeof kwargs === \"object\") {\n    out.chat_template_kwargs = Object.fromEntries(\n      Object.entries(kwargs).map(([key, value]) => [upstream.renameTemplateKwargs![key] ?? key, value]),\n    );\n  }\n  return out;\n}\n\n/** The URL for a client path: /v1/chat/completions on a base of http://h/v1 is http://h/v1/chat/completions. */\nexport function upstreamUrl(baseURL: string, clientPath: string): URL {\n  const base = baseURL.replace(/\\/$/, \"\");\n  return new URL(base + clientPath.replace(/^\\/v1(?=\\/)/, \"\"));\n}\n\nconst HOP_BY_HOP = new Set([\"host\", \"connection\", \"content-length\", \"content-encoding\", \"transfer-encoding\", \"keep-alive\", \"te\", \"trailer\", \"upgrade\", \"proxy-connection\", \"proxy-authorization\"]);\n\nexport function upstreamHeaders(client: IncomingHttpHeaders, protocol: LlmProtocol | null, key: string | undefined): Record<string, string> {\n  const headers: Record<string, string> = {};\n  for (const [name, value] of Object.entries(client)) {\n    if (!HOP_BY_HOP.has(name) && typeof value === \"string\") headers[name] = value;\n  }\n  if (key) {\n    delete headers.authorization;\n    delete headers[\"x-api-key\"];\n    if (protocol === \"anthropic.messages\") headers[\"x-api-key\"] = key;\n    else headers.authorization = `Bearer ${key}`;\n  }\n  return headers;\n}\n\n/** Remembers which upstreams just failed, so a dead one does not cost every request a timeout. */\nexport class Health {\n  private readonly until = new Map<string, number>();\n  constructor(private readonly cooldownMs: number) {}\n  fail(name: string, now = Date.now()): void {\n    this.until.set(name, now + this.cooldownMs);\n  }\n  ok(name: string): void {\n    this.until.delete(name);\n  }\n  /** Healthy members first in their order; cooling ones after, since one may have recovered. */\n  order(members: string[], now = Date.now()): string[] {\n    const cooling = (name: string) => (this.until.get(name) ?? 0) > now;\n    return [...members.filter((name) => !cooling(name)), ...members.filter(cooling)];\n  }\n  cooling(now = Date.now()): string[] {\n    return [...this.until].filter(([, until]) => until > now).map(([name]) => name);\n  }\n}\n\nconst decode = (bytes: Buffer, encoding: string | undefined): Buffer => {\n  switch (encoding) {\n    case \"gzip\": return zlib.gunzipSync(bytes);\n    case \"br\": return zlib.brotliDecompressSync(bytes);\n    case \"deflate\": return zlib.inflateSync(bytes);\n    case \"zstd\": return zlib.zstdDecompressSync(bytes);\n    default: return bytes;\n  }\n};\n\nconst readAll = (stream: IncomingMessage): Promise<Buffer> =>\n  new Promise((resolve, reject) => {\n    const parts: Buffer[] = [];\n    stream.on(\"data\", (part: Buffer) => parts.push(part));\n    stream.on(\"end\", () => resolve(Buffer.concat(parts)));\n    stream.on(\"error\", reject);\n  });\n\n/** Beyond this a reply is forwarded but not sent for judging; a process must not grow without bound. */\nconst MAX_JUDGED_REPLY_BYTES = 64 * 1024 * 1024;\n\n/** What to do with a body once AIRS has answered, from the verdict alone. */\nexport type Judged =\n  | { kind: \"forward\"; body?: Record<string, any> }\n  | { kind: \"answer\"; status: number; contentType: string; body: string; reason: string };\n\n/** The cases of the verdict's `payload`. A `block` with a continuation is a body to carry on with. */\nexport function readVerdict(verdict: Record<string, any>): Judged {\n  const { decision, payload, continuation, payload_stream: stream } = verdict;\n  if (decision === \"block\" && !(continuation && typeof payload === \"object\" && payload && continuation.style !== \"answer\")) {\n    if (typeof payload === \"string\" && stream) return { kind: \"answer\", status: 200, contentType: \"text/event-stream\", body: payload, reason: \"blocked\" };\n    if (payload && typeof payload === \"object\") return { kind: \"answer\", status: 200, contentType: \"application/json\", body: JSON.stringify(payload), reason: \"blocked\" };\n    // Nothing rendered, as for a canonical event: refusing is the only reading of a block.\n    return { kind: \"answer\", status: 403, contentType: \"application/json\", body: JSON.stringify({ error: { message: \"Refused by OpenGuardrails AIRS.\", type: \"openguardrails_blocked\" } }), reason: \"blocked\" };\n  }\n  if (payload && typeof payload === \"object\") return { kind: \"forward\", body: payload };\n  return { kind: \"forward\" };\n}\n\nconst refusal = (message: string): Extract<Judged, { kind: \"answer\" }> => ({\n  kind: \"answer\",\n  status: 503,\n  contentType: \"application/json\",\n  body: JSON.stringify({ error: { message, type: \"openguardrails_fail_closed\" } }),\n  reason: \"fail-closed\",\n});\n\nexport function startGateway(config: Config): Promise<http.Server> {\n  const gateway: Gateway = config.gateway ?? { upstreams: {} };\n  const health = new Health(gateway.cooldownMs ?? 30_000);\n  const connectTimeoutMs = gateway.connectTimeoutMs ?? 5_000;\n  const firstByteTimeoutMs = gateway.firstByteTimeoutMs ?? 600_000;\n  const airs = config.airs;\n  const airsKey = airs ? secretOf(airs) : undefined;\n  const failClosed = airs?.failMode === \"closed\";\n  const requestTimeoutMs = airs?.requestTimeoutMs ?? 6_000;\n  // With AIRS connected, AIRS judges and masks. Otherwise the local guard does.\n  const localRuntime = new LocalRuntime(config);\n  const guard = airsKey ? null : new ModelChannelGuard(localRuntime);\n  let lastFailover: unknown = null;\n  let served = 0;\n  // What runs ask for, since agents reach the gateway directly and their calls never pass the proxy.\n  const seenCalls = new Set<string>();\n  const activity: Array<{ t: number; agent: string; name: string; hosts: string[] }> = [];\n  const blindTo = new Set<string>();\n  const exec = new ExecTracker();\n  // An older AIRS refuses the field. The judgement matters more than the evidence, so it is dropped.\n  let execRefused = false;\n\n  mkdirSync(homeDir(), { recursive: true, mode: 0o700 });\n  // Sandboxed agents can reach this port, so what only `openguardrails run` may do takes a token they cannot read.\n  const internalToken = randomBytes(24).toString(\"hex\");\n  writeFileSync(join(homeDir(), \"gateway.token\"), internalToken, { mode: 0o600 });\n  const log = (type: string, fields: Record<string, unknown>) =>\n    appendFileSync(join(homeDir(), \"gateway.ndjson\"), `${JSON.stringify({ t: new Date().toISOString(), type, ...fields })}\\n`, { mode: 0o600 });\n\n  const identity = (agentType: string) => ({\n    id: airs?.agentId ?? `${agentType}-${hostname()}`,\n    type: agentType,\n    workspace: airs?.agentWorkspace ?? \"\",\n    user: userInfo().username,\n  });\n  const airsUrl = () => new URL(`${airs!.url.replace(/\\/$/, \"\")}/v1/evaluate?payload=true`);\n\n  const noteCalls = (agentType: string, calls: Array<{ id: string; name: string; args: string }>, t: number) => {\n    const opened = [];\n    for (const call of calls) {\n      const hosts = hostsIn(call.args);\n      opened.push({ id: call.id, hosts });\n      if (seenCalls.has(call.id)) continue;\n      seenCalls.add(call.id);\n      activity.push({ t, agent: agentType, name: call.name, hosts });\n      if (activity.length > 5000) activity.shift();\n    }\n    exec.open(opened, t);\n  };\n\n  /** Judges a request before the model sees it. An absent verdict follows the fail mode. */\n  const judgeRequest = async (stepId: string, protocol: LlmProtocol, payload: unknown, agentType: string, endpoint: string, report: ExecReport | undefined): Promise<Judged> => {\n    if (!airsKey) return { kind: \"forward\" };\n    const who = identity(agentType);\n    const event = {\n      kind: \"step/request\", step_id: stepId, agent_id: who.id, agent_type: who.type, agent_workspace: who.workspace,\n      agent_user: who.user, llm_protocol: protocol, payload, integration: INTEGRATION, llm_endpoint: endpoint,\n    };\n    const post = (body: unknown) =>\n      fetch(airsUrl(), {\n        method: \"POST\",\n        headers: { authorization: `Bearer ${airsKey}`, \"content-type\": \"application/json\" },\n        body: JSON.stringify(body),\n        signal: AbortSignal.timeout(requestTimeoutMs),\n      });\n    try {\n      let response = await post(report && !execRefused ? { ...event, exec: report } : event);\n      if (response.status === 400 && report && !execRefused) {\n        const text = await response.text();\n        if (/\\bexec\\b/.test(text)) {\n          execRefused = true;\n          log(\"exec_refused\", { detail: \"this AIRS does not accept the exec field; evidence stays in this log\" });\n          response = await post(event);\n        } else {\n          throw new Error(`HTTP 400 ${text.slice(0, 200)}`);\n        }\n      }\n      const verdict = (await response.json().catch(() => ({}))) as Record<string, any>;\n      // A 200 without a decision is not a verdict.\n      if (!response.ok || !verdict.decision) throw new Error(`HTTP ${response.status}`);\n      log(\"verdict\", { kind: \"step/request\", step: stepId, decision: verdict.decision, findings: verdict.findings?.length ?? 0 });\n      if (failClosed && verdict.unjudged?.length) return refusal(\"OpenGuardrails AIRS could not judge all of this request.\");\n      return readVerdict(verdict);\n    } catch (error) {\n      log(\"verdict\", { kind: \"step/request\", step: stepId, decision: \"unjudged\", error: String(error) });\n      return failClosed ? refusal(\"OpenGuardrails AIRS gave no verdict, and this gateway fails closed.\") : { kind: \"forward\" };\n    }\n  };\n\n  /** Judges a whole, unstreamed reply. Answers what the client should receive. */\n  const judgeWholeReply = async (stepId: string, protocol: LlmProtocol, reply: Buffer, agentType: string, endpoint: string): Promise<{ status?: number; body: Buffer | string; contentType?: string; refused?: boolean }> => {\n    if (!airsKey) return { body: reply };\n    const who = identity(agentType);\n    try {\n      const response = await fetch(airsUrl(), {\n        method: \"POST\",\n        headers: { authorization: `Bearer ${airsKey}`, \"content-type\": \"application/json\" },\n        body: JSON.stringify({\n          kind: \"step/response\", step_id: stepId, agent_id: who.id, agent_type: w